From 50fbe0d8ab8d24c58a172904fa8a55b59531b9a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tarpediem <tarpediem@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:36:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: kexec: no kCFI check on the jump to the relocation
 code

With CONFIG_CFI, kexec -e oopses in machine_kexec(): the indirect call
to kern_reloc first loads the type hash at target - 4 through the idmap
installed in TTBR0, and that address is in the page before the
relocation page, which is not mapped (level 3 translation fault at
kern_reloc - 4, pc machine_kexec+0x12c = ldur w16, [x8, #-4]). The
relocation code is copied from a SYM_CODE block and has no hash anyway.
Mark machine_kexec() __nocfi, as swsusp_arch_resume() already is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c
index 8f9bc2327..e66fbcc9d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c
@@ -159,8 +159,15 @@ int machine_kexec_post_load(struct kimage *kimage)
  * machine_kexec - Do the kexec reboot.
  *
  * Called from the core kexec code for a sys_reboot with LINUX_REBOOT_CMD_KEXEC.
+ *
+ * __nocfi: both calls below go through a physical address. With CONFIG_CFI,
+ * the indirect call to kern_reloc first loads the type hash 4 bytes before
+ * the target, in the page before the relocation page, which the idmap in
+ * TTBR0 does not map: a translation fault in machine_kexec(). The relocation
+ * code is copied from an untyped SYM_CODE block, so there is no hash to match
+ * anyway. swsusp_arch_resume() does the same for the same reason.
  */
-void machine_kexec(struct kimage *kimage)
+void __nocfi machine_kexec(struct kimage *kimage)
 {
 	bool in_kexec_crash = (kimage == kexec_crash_image);
 	bool stuck_cpus = cpus_are_stuck_in_kernel();
-- 
2.56.0

